## Bench reproducibility (Step 1)
| encoder     | bytes  | bfly  | ssim2 | Δ% vs cjxl | ΔSSIM2 vs cjxl |
|---          |---     |---    |---    |---         |---             |
| cjxl 0.12.0 | 62,710 | 2.991 | 84.86 | (baseline) | (baseline)     |
| Libjxl-ours | 70,217 | 3.209 | 79.35 | +11.97%    | -5.51          |
| Zenjxl-ours | 62,850 | 3.216 | 80.53 | +0.22%     | -4.33          |

Reproduces AUDIT-4 (`0e65668f`) exactly. The +12pp "structural" Libjxl-strategy gap
is confirmed.

Critical observation: Libjxl-strategy is STRICTLY WORSE than Zenjxl-strategy
on this cell (more bytes AND lower SSIM2). The deficit Δbetween = -1.18 SSIM2
+ 11.7pp bytes is purely caused by the Libjxl-only divergences (Section A
effort-gates + Section D KNOWN-BUG re-enables + Section C CfL Newton parity).

